nd in Ukraine is highly  volatile Russian backed separatists have  NX Crimea keeping military installations  from enemy view makes strategic sense  clandestine military bases are often  seen tucked away in remote parts of  forests analysts scour the rest of the  image for possible signs of military  activity but find none  there don't seem to be enough roads or  rail lines or even an airfield for it to  be a substantial military base research  into historical image archives produces  an unredacted photo of the same area the  older photograph reveals what is hiding  beneath the white blotches  it's a massive parking lot but why is it  there you see choppers and trucks parked  in the clearing what could be so special  about them that somebody wanted scrubbed  from the image  the deserted roadways of Chernobyl and  the nearby town of Pripyat offer a clue  it's like a post-apocalyptic scene from  a videogame the buildings are in place  the school is in place the amusement  park is in place but there's no cars no  trucks no buses  they've all been removed the Soviet  government knew that they had thousands  and thousands of irradiated vehicles and  the last thing that they wanted was  people taking these contaminated cars  and trucks and driving them all over the  Soviet Union or simply parked in the  middle of forests and big fence put  around it and keep out signs put up the  white blotches mask the deadliest  parking lot on the planet where over a  thousand irradiated vehicles have been  left to rot the medals themselves can't  be washed off these will be very  dangerous for thousands of years to come  the lethal threat posed by the  radioactive vehicles is supposed to be  contained but security is lacs and  potentially deadly radioactivity is  spreading beyond the containment area  people's garbage these vehicles for  metal or parts or whatever to be able to  sell them on the black market or to  recyclers people were coming in and  stripping off car parts and selling